+## LV7b (levels audio kit: 6 songs, 12 sound effects): resident delta 0 B
+
+Nothing of the kit is on the PS1 yet. `SONG_COUNT` and `SFX_SYNTH_END` (audio.h) keep their old values there (as `TEX_COUNT`
+does), the six song rows, their unlock rows and the 12 effect recipes are compiled out, and `core/gen/mus_data.c` holds two
+copies of the music bank: the PS1 picks the old bank, byte for byte (`tools/mmlc.py` builds it without the late cues and the
+test of the old golden hashes still compares it). The 12 effects are synth one-shots (0 B of PCM), so `SFX.BIN` (47,793 B of PCM,
+24 sectors) and the SPU map (SFX 0x2000-0x2FFFF, Talk 0x30000-0x7DFFF) do not change either. A new song id plays as "no song"
+here. The switch is the same one as the levels' `LV_HAS_NEW`: it comes with PS1-RAM. Share of 8 KB resident used by LV7b: 0 B.
